Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:01:35 -0600
Subject: upstream-pr-2621: games/0400C3F00006E000: register Mario Kart World
 1.8.0's build row, and report a registered update packed with its own shader
 tables as registered

The profile registered only the base game (v0), so a 1.8.0 (v917504) NUP was packed from a derived profile with `[RED] ... was not brought up on` and an unknown display version.

- game.tsv: `build v917504 1.8.0` with the four modules' build IDs, read from the files of a v917504 NUP (main d00e4f39, subsdk0 746302f4, subsdk1 8dec9c0b, sdk 7a68b13d). `package` and `shader_versions` stay v0: the shader tables are the base game's, so 1.8.0 still gets a derived profile for its own shaders, which now carries the registered display version (1.8.0, not "?").
- scripts/build_ipa_from_nsp.py report_profile_status: it compared the derived profile's whole build table with the registered one. A derived profile keeps only the packed version's row, so a game registering more than one build never matched and the registered update was still red. It compares the packed version's own row now; a module the profile does not register is red as before.
- dm/tools/tests/test_nsp_registered_update.py: a registered update is reported as registered, with no red line (fails without the change), and an unregistered one is red.
- Notes: the game note's 1.8.0 section says what the registration reaches. This game has no fixed-address cuts (the frame step is function-matched, applied to 1.8.0 at main+0x69cc54) and no host code keyed to its build IDs, so there was nothing to carry from v0's main with nso_fnmap.py. Open: the two SDK-wide address-region patches match no function in SDK 21.4.0 and are not applied; the region check passes without them, later play is not measured.

Checked: test_docs, test_game_profile, test_patches, test_nso_match, test_nsp_alias / dump / aarch64 / chain / registered_update; derive_profile and report_profile_status run on the real 1.8.0 extraction (display 1.8.0, no red line). Not run: regress.py, lint_python (ruff not installed), a full rebuild with the change, iOS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
