 - the game reloads one asset for ever: a background loader takes about a core and the process several (Ocarina of Time: 412% CPU on the Mac, `OptimizeChangeBanc` and `ParallelDecompThread` busy all session, one model and its texture opened about 22 times a second). Or, from the NSP script: `vN: K file(s) whose bytes do not start as their names promise (a .zs file that is not a zstd stream), so the game files are damaged`, then the files. → [A damaged file in a NUP or a dump has no hash to fail](../reference/packing.md#a-damaged-file-in-a-nup-or-a-dump-has-no-hash-to-fail)
 - `pack_nup.py`, or the NSP script on a NUP, ends in a Python traceback (`RecursionError` in `tree_bytes`) instead of a `[RED]` line. → [A NUP whose folder contains itself](../reference/packing.md#a-nup-whose-folder-contains-itself)
